# Nothing under build/ is source. It is all produced by ./build.sh or the
# QEMU harness and can be regenerated: ISOs, the live-build chroot, VM disks
# and firmware variables, logs, screenshots and the approval previews.
# Screenshots in particular are test evidence, not code - they are large and
# they can capture whatever happened to be on the screen.
build/

# Caches and disk images, wherever they end up. There is deliberately no
# bare "chroot/" rule: it matched hooks/chroot/ as well, so every hook file
# added after it was silently untracked. build/ already covers the real
# live-build chroot.
*.iso
*.iso.sha256
*.img
*.squashfs
*.qcow2
*.vmdk
*.fd
.cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Bashan app source/archive: never in git, never in the ISO
assets/apps/

# Large source assets stay local; only generated branding is tracked
assets/_extra-copies/

# Secrets
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.gpg
*.asc
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519
secrets/
.env
.env.*

# ...except these two, which are PUBLIC apt signing keys. They are not
# secrets: they are how apt verifies Brave's and Google's packages, and the
# build needs them. Without this exception the *.key rule above silently
# drops them and the archives stop verifying.
!config/archives/brave-browser.key
!config/archives/google-chrome.key.binary

# Editor / OS noise
*~
.*.swp
.DS_Store

# Artwork and notes whose rights or contents are not for publication.
# Local-only: kept in ~/bashan-private-assets and staged into private builds
# by scripts/27-private-assets.sh. A clone builds without them.
theme/wallpapers/bashan-mountain-*.png
assets/reference/
assets/audio/
branding/boot-song/
installer/branding/bashan/welcome.png
docs/legal/BLOCKS-PUBLIC-RELEASE.md
